   "scion_answer": "Let's define variables for the number of tennis balls retrieved in each set:\n- Let x = number of balls retrieved in the first set\n- Let y = number of balls retrieved in the second set\n- Let z = number of balls retrieved in the third set\n\nFrom the problem statement:\n1. **First set**: He retrieved four more balls than in the second set \u2192 x = y + 4\n2. **Third set**: He retrieved half as many balls as in the second \u2192 z = y/2\n3. **Total**: He retrieved 19 tennis balls in all \u2192 x + y + z = 19\n\nSubstituting into the total equation:\n(y + 4) + y + (y/2) = 19\n2y + y/2 + 4 = 19\n5y/2 = 15\ny = 6\n\nTherefore:\n- First set: x = 6 + 4 = **10**\n- Second set: y = 6\n- Third set: z = 6/2 = 3\n\nCheck: 10 + 6 + 3 = 19 \u2713\n\nFinal answer: 10",
